AWS Security Incident Report

1. Incident Overview

Project: AWS Cloud Security Monitoring and Threat Detection System
Environment: AWS – us-east-1
Incident Type: Simulated security finding
Detection Service: Amazon GuardDuty
Alerting Services: Amazon EventBridge and Amazon SNS
Status: Investigated – Simulation

2. Detection

Amazon GuardDuty generated sample security findings to test the monitoring system.

The findings were detected by GuardDuty and matched an EventBridge rule configured to receive GuardDuty security findings.

Amazon SNS delivered an email notification confirming that the alerting pipeline was working.

3. Investigation Process

The following steps were used:

Opened the GuardDuty console.
Reviewed the generated sample findings.
Examined the finding details and severity.
Verified that EventBridge received the finding.
Confirmed that SNS delivered the email notification.

4. Recommended Response

For a real security incident, the response would depend on the finding and affected resource.

Recommended actions include:

Validate the finding and identify the affected AWS resource.
Review related CloudTrail events.
Determine whether unauthorized activity occurred.
Contain compromised resources or credentials when appropriate.
Restore affected resources and strengthen security controls.
Document the investigation and resolution.

5. Test Results
  Result: Successful.

GuardDuty sample findings generated.
EventBridge rule configured and enabled.
SNS email subscription confirmed.
Email alert successfully received.

6. Conclusion

This project demonstrates an AWS security monitoring workflow using managed detection, event-driven alerting, and centralized audit logging.

The test used simulated findings and does not represent a confirmed real-world security incident.
